WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.780
Fight, crash through, and face the challenge!

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.000
These are our hard knock days.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Can't quench our thirst with a peaceful, everyday life.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
Here we go - don't ever run away!

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.380
Let's go on living as the mighty winds take us!

7
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.870
We've still got so far to go.

8
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.390
Gotta keep going through the hard knock days.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.610
Let's do it again, yes, baby. How many times

10
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.110
do I have to stand back up to make my dream come true?

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
Feels like the strength of my resolve

12
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
is put to the test everyday.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey, let's go!

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.450
I don't want to make excuses and settle for being mediocre.

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.960
Hey, let's go!

16
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.670
We leapt into a crazy, lawless world.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.170
As I struggled for a foothold, reality caught me off guard.

18
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.470
Even if it beats me, hits me, knocks me down again,

19
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.220
Oh!

20
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.560
Only when we get back on our feet and look forward,

21
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.450
will we have the last laugh, be the winners!

22
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.120
We gotta go down this glory road, till we reach our goal!

23
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.720
Fight, shake it off, act strong!

24
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.720
These are our hard knock days.

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.730
There's no such thing as a safe choice.

26
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.060
Here we go - we'll always be the strongest!

27
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.320
Let's keep moving - never mind the consequences.

28
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.900
Let's put our wishes all together,

29
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.910
and keep on going through the hard knock days.

30
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>To Russian, With Love</b>

31
00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:51.710
Nico Robin, you insolent little...

32
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.660
Don't you think they were
a little too disadvantaged?

33
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.550
Disadvantaged?

34
00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:02.680
Hey, now... do you really think this is meant to be a fair duel or something?

35
00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.680
This is an execution, Nico Robin!

36
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.980
I think you have that backwards.

37
00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.740
Commander-san, you no longer need to look over your shoulder.

38
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.450
I'll stay with Rebecca!

39
00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.710
Thank you, I'm in your debt.

40
00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.660
I was just about to be overwhelmed...

41
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.370
with rage!

42
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.050
<b>Palace Plateau
Third Step</b>

43
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.300
What are you guys doing?!

44
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.680
Have mercy!

45
00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.060
W-We're just carrying away the corpse of the fallen! Please let us go!

46
00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.480
He's not dead yet!

47
00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.720
You're right.

48
00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:59.030
And it might take days before he wakes up again, but we want to look after him!

49
00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.570
Please! Have a warrior's mercy!

50
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.530
Please have mercy!

51
00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.740
I'm begging you!

52
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.370
Okay, fine! Just go already!

53
00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.240
Thank you very much!

54
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.490
Jeez...

55
00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.070
<b>The Smile Factory</b>

56
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.490
Oh, Senor!

57
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.020
It got through!

58
00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.500
Viola-sama, this is the factory team!

59
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.020
What's going on with Princess Mansherry and Leo's group?

60
00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:35.060
The princess might be going through a horrible ordeal as we speak!

61
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.980
I'm so worried!

62
00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.040
I just found out something terrible.

63
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:41.820
Something terrible?!

64
00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.580
Wait a moment.
I'll call Leo now, so stay on the line.

65
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.950
<b>Former Royal Plateau</b>

66
00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.560
Leo, can you hear me?

67
00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.120
Oh, Viola-sama!

68
00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.330
We're on our way up the rampart tower now!

69
00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.470
We'll reach the chapel in the palace soon!

70
00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.570
Leo, you have to hurry!

71
00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:04.140
Giolla is holding Mansherry, and is forcing her to use her ability!

72
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.680
What? That's awful!

73
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.820
Oh no! Hurry up, Leo!

74
00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:14.040
<b>The Rampart Tower Underneath the Royal Palace</b>

75
00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.700
There they are! Dwarfs!

76
00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.020
They're coming up!

77
00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.730
Fire, fire!

78
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.670
<b>The Stairway to the Royal Palace</b>

79
00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.320
Bring the bombs! I'll blow them away along with the stairway!

80
00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.660
We'll get there in a super hurry!

81
00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.040
Hang on a little bit more, Princess Mansherry!

82
00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.710
Listen to me already...

83
00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.590
princess of the Dwarfs!

84
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.600
<b>Behind the Chapel, First Floor
 The Punishment Room</b>

85
00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.950
I can't do it anymore...

86
00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:51.020
<b>The Tontatta Chief's Daughter and Princess of the Tontattans
Mansherry</b>

87
00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.940
Let me go back to Green Bit!

88
00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:58.340
I can't help you anymore!

89
00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.820
Silence!

90
00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.500
Who did you call Boa Hancock?!

91
00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.940
I-I never... said anything like...

92
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.910
Don't be such a baby!

93
00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.960
It's time to unleash your ability!

94
00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.420
Look!

95
00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.520
Look at the fallen commanders!

96
00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:28.260
The people who fought against our commanders, however...

97
00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.310
They may have been victorious,
but they were gravely injured in their fights.

98
00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:41.230
If you resuscitate the commanders with your Healing Fruit power,

99
00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:45.530
our foes will be powerless, and have to accept their own deaths!

100
00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.400
The battle will be completely turned in our favor!

101
00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.420
Now,

102
00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:58.580
use the ability that recovered Sugar earlier again!

103
00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:02.710
Take out the watering can filled with magic water!

104
00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.060
Now! Now!

105
00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.090
Now!

106
00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.680
I've learned...

107
00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:20.730
that you're bad people who caused trouble for King Riku...

108
00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:26.130
and that King Doflamingo is lying to us.

109
00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:30.140
So what?! Stop acting so high and mighty, you brazen Tontattan!

110
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:37.140
I don't want to cure bad people anymore!

111
00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:39.830
So...

112
00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.190
So adorable!

113
00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:51.200
Adorable!

114
00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.930
Hey, stay focused!

115
00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.680
Who did you call the once-in-a-millennium beauty?!

116
00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.900
Now!

117
00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.530
Help!

118
00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.500
Well then...

119
00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.720
I take it you don't care what happens to your friends at the factory?

120
00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:19.910
B-But if I heal their wounds, they'll just hurt somebody again, won't they?!

121
00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:21.530
You cheeky little brat!

122
00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:25.460
I'll do whatever it takes to squeeze the power out of you!

123
00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:29.590
Help me, Leo!

124
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.470
I hit one!

125
00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.010
Kabu-san!

126
00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:38.470
Kabu-san?! Leo! What happened to him?!

127
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.430
Don't stop!

128
00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.300
Go ahead, Leo!

129
00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.830
I'll catch up with you soon! I'm okay!

130
00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.050
That hurts! You're hurting me!

131
00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.900
What happened to me?

132
00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.350
His injuries were healed!

133
00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.700
I see, princess of the Dwarfs.

134
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.820
I guess you can heal wounds with your tears, too.

135
00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.330
Cry some more!

136
00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.460
No!

137
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.880
Come on! Shed more healing tears!

138
00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.470
It hurts! Help!

139
00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.050
Leo, hurry!

140
00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.050
Right away!

141
00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.770
What's wrong, Viola?!

142
00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.520
Giolla noticed Mansherry's tears can heal wounds!

143
00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.020
What?!

144
00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:10.480
She's beating her cruelly to make her shed tears!

145
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.440
What?!

146
00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.520
Princess!

147
00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.120
I, Mousey, will come save you now!

148
00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:22.620
It's no use! We have to count on Leo and Kabu-san for now!

149
00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.920
The princess of the Tontattas has the power to heal?!

150
00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.480
She ate the Healing Fruit.

151
00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:35.470
The basis of its power is healing wounds of living things.

152
00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:38.000
No wonder the enemy wants it.

153
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.140
Indeed.

154
00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:45.160
They're trying to use that power to bring the fallen commanders back to full strength!

155
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.230
If they do, we're done for!

156
00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.150
This is super bad!

157
00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.610
Leo, we're counting on you!

158
00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:55.360
Kabu-san, hang in there!

159
00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.950
But Sugar isn't with them, right?

160
00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:01.910
She is!

161
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.790
Whaaat?!

162
00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.010
They're coming back?! You've got to be kidding!

163
00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.640
You can do it, Leo!

164
00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.530
Go! Take back the princess!

165
00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.430
Indeed!

166
00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.000
There it is! The punishment room!

167
00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.410
I found her!

168
00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.540
Leo!

169
00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.250
Princess!

170
00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.830
You're too late!

171
00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.170
Get him!

172
00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.680
Now, come back, commanders of the Donquixote Family!

173
00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.440
Round Two, begins!

174
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.100
Leo!

175
00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.400
Outta my way!

176
00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.360
You take care of Giolla!

177
00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.250
Beetle...

178
00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.830
Uppercut!

179
00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.300
What?!

180
00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:38.180
Sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew!

181
00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.270
Sew!

182
00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:43.850
Sew...

183
00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:46.060
Sew, sew, sew, sew, sew!

184
00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:55.070
I'll line them up and try again!

185
00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:57.120
There's no need!

186
00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.830
Sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew!

187
00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.330
Sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew, sew...

188
00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.960
What?!

189
00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.380
I'll sew you all up together so you'll never get separated!

190
00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:20.600
What is this?!

191
00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.890
Haute Couture!

192
00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.890
High Class Sewing

193
00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.730
Patchwork!

194
00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:27.200
What?!

195
00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:47.290
Leo came to save me...

196
00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.590
He's like a prince!

197
00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.690
It... is... art...

198
00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.640
<b>Former Royal Plateau</b>

199
00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.690
He made it! That was really close!

200
00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:14.030
R-Really?!

201
00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:18.150
He finished off Giolla before she could restore anyone!

202
00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.490
Small person, a job well done!

203
00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:24.340
Mansherry has been saved!

204
00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:27.710
Yeah!

205
00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:36.260
Leo, I was scared...

206
00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:43.180
Princess, you gained some weight again.

207
00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:49.070
The Tontattan Princess, Mansherry
Rescued successfully

208
00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.270
Same old...

209
00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:54.940
Leo! Leo!

210
00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.600
I hurt my leg.

211
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.450
You can carry me on your back if you want!

212
00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.890
Or you can carry me in your arms, that works too.

213
00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.140
There it is! The Princess' selfishness!

214
00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:14.140
If you really were hurt, you could heal yourself!

215
00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:20.090
You've always been a good runner,
so let's just run and get out of here!

216
00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:23.890
Then I'm not going anywhere.

217
00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.340
What?! There it is!

218
00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.040
The Princess' entitlement!

219
00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.930
It's not like I want your help anyway.

220
00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.900
What's with that attitude?!

221
00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.640
I really will leave you here!

222
00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.350
Fine by me!

223
00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.540
Just carry her on your back already!

224
00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.440
We gotta go!

225
00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.410
Ow...

226
00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:53.290
Honestly!
You're selfish, entitled, and quick-tempered...

227
00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.720
You're such a bother, Princess!

228
00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.930
Leo's back...

229
00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:03.570
She's nice to everyone besides him.

230
00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.930
How dense are you, Leo?

231
00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.340
This is awful!

232
00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.150
They stole Mansherry away! Catch those Dwarfs!

233
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:18.320
They went that way! Don't let them get away!

234
00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.390
I... I failed...

235
00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:24.780
But this is a crisis!

236
00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:28.830
I have to report this to the young master!

237
00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:33.540
Mansherry's ultimate ability is essential to the young master's plan.

238
00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:39.170
Her ability to restore things
in exchange for shortening her life!

239
00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:43.170
Even if something happens to the Smile factory,

240
00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.680
as long as we have the Healing Fruit power on our side,

241
00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:51.520
we can restore it. I'm sure that's what he's thinking!

242
00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.360
If nothing is done, th-th...

243
00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:00.960
The factory will be destroyed!

244
00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:00.690
<b>The SMILE Factory</b>

245
00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:04.360
<b>Franky vs. Senor Pink</b>

246
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.950
Senor, defend the factory at all costs!

247
00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.950
Franky...

248
00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:10.200
No! Dodge, Senor!

249
00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.870
Strong...

250
00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:14.870
Hammer!

251
00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.860
Oh! He dove into the ground again!

252
00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.240
Fraland, he's gonna do it again!

253
00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:27.930
Dodge!

254
00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:32.520
Meow-Meow...

255
00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.310
Suplex!

256
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.740
Oh! Senor!

257
00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.210
Neither of them can keep this up!

258
00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.960
Fraland!

259
00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:04.820
I know you could have dodged that attack, Fraland!

260
00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:08.090
You've taken that same attack thirty times in a row now! Why?!

261
00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.530
Stay out of this, Tontattans.

262
00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:17.270
Yeah... Senor took the same punch thirty times too.

263
00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.160
Why is that?!

264
00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.500
When somebody offers you a drink at a bar,

265
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:26.940
if you're a real man, you don't pull your glass away!

266
00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.250
What?! Then, don't tell me you were...

267
00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:33.420
This guy is one staunch dude. So I...

268
00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.830
will not try to avoid a single attack he throws at me.

269
00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:41.380
I'll take all of his attacks head-on, and still win at the end!

270
00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:46.770
That's my... Strong-style!

271
00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:51.920
I know you're worried, but this is a manly duel!

272
00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.560
I'll win no matter what, so just you watch!

273
00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:59.770
I won't let you guys become their slaves again!

274
00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:06.810
Fraland!

275
00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:13.570
You make me drunker than some cheap bar, kid.

276
00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.750
Don't forget what you just said!

277
00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.750
I'm...

278
00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.990
not exactly young anymore.

279
00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:26.620
Let me end it with this next move.

280
00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.910
Senor, can I say one thing before that?!

281
00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:31.970
You're far away! Way too far away!

282
00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:37.060
You understand what I'm getting at, right?

283
00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:41.230
You said you'd take all my attacks head-on.

284
00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:46.400
If you want to live up to your manly declaration,
then take this and...

285
00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.400
try staying alive!

286
00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:59.910
If, against all odds,
you manage to get back up afterwards, I've lost.

287
00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.830
I'll take your final attack head-on!

288
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.300
Fine by me!

289
00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.830
He's swimming through the wall of the tower!

290
00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.160
What is he up to?!

291
00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:27.520
Unfortunately, the sky isn't particularly friendly today.

292
00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.570
Otherwise, if I kept going up,

293
00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:32.450
I'd be able to see Russian.

294
00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:33.980
Russian?

295
00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:37.610
Yeah... I have a son named Gimlet, too.

296
00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:44.950
But unfortunately, gravity persists. I can't keep going up.

297
00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.290
Hey! What are you talking about?!

298
00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:51.050
Cyborg, your back is flesh and blood, isn't it?

299
00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.630
You... figured that out?!

300
00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.340
Now, stop talking!

301
00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.300
Or you'll bite your own tongue off!

302
00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:04.700
Meow-Meow Suplex!

303
00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:10.700
Baby...

304
00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.530
Buster!

305
00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:45.430
Fraland!

306
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.030
You gave me your word...

307
00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:00.440
so it's my turn now!

308
00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.450
I've lost.

309
00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.920
Sorry, young master.

310
00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.380
Franky...

311
00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:15.420
Iron Boxing!

312
00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:16.970
Oh, right...

313
00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:18.510
Russian...

314
00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:23.760
The day that I met you...
and the day that you stopped smiling...

315
00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:34.530
They were both nights of pouring rain like this...

316
00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:43.420
The rain came out of nowhere, didn't it? I'm soaked!

317
00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:47.540
You're soaking wet, but you're smiling?

318
00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:52.030
I... like rain.

319
00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:59.880
Things that I don't like? Hmm...

320
00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:02.890
Oh, pirates! I hate them to death!

321
00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:06.480
What do you do for a living? C'mon, tell me.

322
00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:10.480
I-I work at a bank.

323
00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:12.650
Really...

324
00:22:22.510 --> 00:22:23.700
Darling!

325
00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:29.910
Well, Darling, what should we name him?

326
00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:31.190
Let's see...

327
00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:33.400
Gimlet.

328
00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:35.380
That's a great name!

329
00:23:06.490 --> 00:23:07.080
What?

330
00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.750
Gimlet died?

331
00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:15.340
A week ago today, the day you left without notice,

332
00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.000
his temperature went up suddenly...

333
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.630
and I took him to the hospital,
but there was nothing they could do!

334
00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:25.090
Liar...

335
00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:25.640
What?

336
00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:27.720
Liar!

337
00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:30.470
I called the bank several times!

338
00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.100
And they said they didn't have anyone like you working for them!

339
00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:36.020
Please! Tell me the truth!

340
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.980
What do you really do for a living?!

341
00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:41.210
What kind of money are we living on?!

342
00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:42.320
Answer me!

343
00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:45.450
Come on! Can't you answer?!

344
00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:48.660
You're not worthy to be a father anymore!

345
00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:50.430
Get out of my way!

346
00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:52.000
W-Wait!

347
00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:56.080
Wait, Russian! It's still stormy outside!

348
00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:58.290
Do you take me for a fool?!

349
00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:00.420
Don't follow me!

350
00:24:03.610 --> 00:24:05.550
It's not what you think, Russian...

351
00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:08.890
The reason I can't tell you everything is...

352
00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:10.470
Russian!

353
00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:11.840
Where are you?!

354
00:24:12.730 --> 00:24:14.400
Russian!

355
00:24:20.030 --> 00:24:21.870
Because of the rain,

356
00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:26.910
there was a mudslide right above your wife,
and she was caught in it.

357
00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:29.680
Her condition is quite serious.

358
00:24:30.370 --> 00:24:32.550
In a vegetative state?

359
00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:35.340
Yes, she is unconscious.

360
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:38.410
I'm sorry, but the way things are now,

361
00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:42.630
she'll probably never be able to express her feelings again.

362
00:24:43.610 --> 00:24:46.590
I don't know how long her body can last, either...

363
00:24:46.590 --> 00:24:50.050
If only you hadn't met me, you would've...

364
00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:52.390
Thank you, Darling!

365
00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:57.580
I'm sorry! I didn't wanna lose you...

366
00:24:58.200 --> 00:25:00.730
So I lied!

367
00:25:03.480 --> 00:25:05.250
I want to hear her respond...

368
00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:11.040
I want to hear her voice...

369
00:25:13.070 --> 00:25:14.330
One more time...

370
00:25:14.650 --> 00:25:16.160
Just one more time...

371
00:25:16.820 --> 00:25:18.680
I want her to smile.

372
00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:23.400
One more time...

373
00:25:24.980 --> 00:25:26.400
Russian, look.

374
00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:29.180
I found the same bonnet that Gimlet used to wear!

375
00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:31.910
Well, do I look like him?

376
00:25:31.910 --> 00:25:33.620
He took after me, and all.

377
00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:37.740
I-I'm sorry! I went too far with that joke.

378
00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:40.000
If someone sees me wearing this...

379
00:25:50.370 --> 00:25:51.890
Russian.

380
00:26:23.790 --> 00:26:25.120
You're one hell of a character, old man!

381
00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:28.460
He lost his son, and his wife was in a terrible accident.

382
00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:31.930
That's enough to break anyone.

383
00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:42.380
Pink, what the hell happened to your fashion sense?!

384
00:26:42.380 --> 00:26:43.220
Hey!

385
00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:46.180
I'm going out.

386
00:26:47.330 --> 00:26:49.370
Look! It's a pervert!

387
00:26:49.370 --> 00:26:51.010
Pervert passing through!

388
00:26:51.010 --> 00:26:52.500
Disgusting!

389
00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:53.480
Oh! It's a freak!

390
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:54.880
Hey! Stop that!

391
00:27:11.860 --> 00:27:13.000
Russian...

392
00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:18.410
To me,

393
00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:25.820
these outfits are more valuable than the finest suits money can buy.

394
00:27:32.570 --> 00:27:34.930
Because the times I wear these outfits...

395
00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:39.700
are the only times you smile for me.

396
00:28:05.480 --> 00:28:07.060
Senor!

397
00:28:07.060 --> 00:28:09.450
Fraland!

398
00:28:25.230 --> 00:28:27.610
Pathetic.

399
00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:31.430
Just what could you be recalling...

400
00:28:31.430 --> 00:28:34.230
that made you cry like that?

401
00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:35.480
Brother.

402
00:28:53.480 --> 00:28:57.230
If we meet again someday, somewhere...

403
00:28:58.050 --> 00:28:59.750
Let's have a drink,

404
00:29:00.610 --> 00:29:02.830
and then you can tell me...

405
00:29:04.070 --> 00:29:08.180
about that woman, Russian.

406
00:29:09.030 --> 00:29:12.530
The battle at the Smile Factory

407
00:29:12.530 --> 00:29:14.410
Winner: Franky
